# Lenovo IdeaPad Slim 3 15ABR8 - Core Control Suite

**Core Control Suite** is a low-level automation utility, background shortcut manager, and telemetry monitor built specifically for the **Lenovo IdeaPad Slim 3 15ABR8** laptop running Windows 11. 

The project follows a modular architecture utilizing **CustomTkinter** for the graphical user interface, the **WinRT API** for native OS integration, and a custom asynchronous string-based command interpreter implemented in `hotcases.py`.

---

## 🚀 Hardware Trigger Specification (Scan Codes)

In addition to standard key combinations (e.g., `ctrl+alt+x`), the engine supports direct low-level interception of the laptop's dedicated hardware buttons via their system **Scan Codes**:

*   **`183`** — Dedicated Calculator hardware button (co-located with `F12`). Registering this code completely intercepts and blocks the default Windows calculator popup (`suppress=True`) and executes your custom defined event instead.

---

## 📜 Full Syntax & Event Engine Command Catalog

The engine supports two execution modes: **Single System Commands** and **Conditional Statements (IF-THEN-ELSE)**.

### 1. Single Base Commands

| Command & Syntax | Description | Example Usage |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`open "<app_name_or_path>"`** | Launches an application via the Windows system `PATH` environment variable or using a direct path to the `.exe` file. It is recommended to use the `start` prefix to ensure stable GUI execution. | `open "start chrome"`<br>`open "notepad"`<br>`open "C:\Program Files\..."` |
| **`url "<link>"`** | Instantly opens the specified web address using the default system web browser. | `url "https://github.com"`<br>`url "https://google.com"` |
| **`cmd "<cli_command>"`** | Spawns a new Command Prompt (`cmd.exe`) window and executes the specified CLI instruction within the current project directory. | `cmd "git status"`<br>`cmd "docker-compose up"` |
| **`kill "<process_name.exe>"`** | Forcefully terminates the specified process along with its entire process tree, bypassing any OS confirmation dialogs (`taskkill /F /T`). | `kill "chrome.exe"`<br>`kill "discord.exe"` |
| **`toast "<message_text>"`** | Displays a native, modern Windows 11 toast notification banner in the bottom-right corner of the screen using the WinRT API via the `win11toast` library. | `toast "Project compiled successfully!"` |

---

### 2. Conditional Statements (`IF-THEN-ELSE`)

The scripting engine continuously monitors the state of Windows processes and the laptop's hardware sensors in real-time.

#### A. Process Activity Checks (`Process Condition`)
Allows creating **cyclic toggle shortcuts** (Toggle Switches). If the target process is currently active, one action is performed; otherwise, an alternate action is executed.
*   **Syntax:** `if process "<name.exe>" running then <command> [else <command>]`
*   **Example:**
    ```text
    if process "chrome.exe" running then kill "chrome.exe" else open "start chrome"
    ```

#### B. Hardware Telemetry Checks (`Hardware Conditions`)
The engine has direct programmatic access to the laptop's power and performance subsystems. The following live variables are available:
*   `cpu` — Current AMD Ryzen CPU utilization layer in % (integer from 0 to 100).
*   `battery` — Current battery charge capacity state in % (integer from 0 to 100).
*   `charging` — AC power grid connection state (`True` — charging/plugged in, `False` — discharging/running on battery).

**Examples of Use:**
*   **Critical Battery Power Control:**
    ```text
    if battery < 20 and not charging then toast "Battery low! Please connect your Lenovo power adapter!"
    ```
*   **CPU Thermal / Throttling Monitoring:**
    ```text
    if cpu > 85 then toast "Warning! Ryzen processor is under extreme utilization!"
    ```

---

## 💾 Configuration Database Structure (`config.json`)

All created hotkeys and mapped dynamic rules are automatically serialized into a structured `config.json` file located in the application root directory. You can edit them via the GUI manager tab or modify them manually using any raw text editor:

```json
{
  "ctrl+alt+x": "open \"code\"",
  "183": "if cpu > 80 then toast \"Ryzen thermal load is high!\" else cmd \"git status\"",
  "ctrl+alt+t": "if battery < 25 and not charging then toast \"Low battery state detected!\" else open \"cmd\"",
  "ctrl+1+c": "if process \"chrome.exe\" running then toast \"chrome is running\" else open \"start chrome\""
}
```

---

## 🛠️ System Requirements & Dependencies

To ensure stable background loop operations, UI rendering, and native Windows 11 notifications, the following packages must be installed in your python environment:

```bash
pip install customtkinter wmi psutil keyboard pystray pillow win11toast
```

*Note: Accessing certain low-level system variables (such as checking the Secure Boot status in the UEFI NVRAM) may require running the main `monitor.py` script with administrator privileges.*
